%N A399337 The binomial matrix of the central Delannoy numbers, square array read by ascending antidiagonals.
%C A399337 See the comments and links in A399000.
%H A399337 Peter Luschny, <a href="https://github.com/PeterLuschny/Gists/blob/main/GnomonicExpansionAndBinomialMatrices.ipynb">Gnomonic Expansion and Binomial Matrices</a>, a Python notebook.
%F A399337 A(n, n) = D(n) := A001850(n), the central Delannoy numbers.
%F A399337 A(n, k) = Sum_{m=0..d} binomial(d, m) * s^(d - m) * D(p + m), where d = abs(n - k), p = min(n, k), s = 1 if k <= n, otherwise -1.
